# Tasks

## 1. Value schema: record owner or type owner

- [x] 1.1 Migration of `content_values_*` (all seven tables): `content_node_id` and `content_node_uuid` become nullable, `entity` is added (`'node'` by default; existing rows stay `node`), CHECK `(entity='node' AND node_id/uuid NOT NULL) OR (entity='type' AND node_id/uuid NULL)` and `UNIQUE ((COALESCE(content_node_id, 0)), content_type, field_key, lang, weight)`; a branch for MySQL and SQLite, raw SQL for the CHECK and the index, `down()` deletes the rows of the type, the index, the CHECK and `entity`. Check `docker compose exec app php artisan migrate:fresh` (MySQL), the reverse `migrate:rollback --step=1` and `php artisan test` on SQLite without new failures
- [x] 1.2 Feature test of the schema (`tests/Feature/Content/TypeValuesSchemaTest.php`): a row of a type with `content_node_id = NULL` is saved (the FK of the record does not interfere); a `node` row without a record and a `type` row with a record are rejected by the CHECK; a duplicate (type, field, language, weight) for a type is rejected by the index, and for a record it remains rejected by the old unique; deleting a type cascades to delete its rows. Check that `docker compose exec app php artisan test --filter=TypeValuesSchema` is green
- [x] 1.3 Update the documentation in Ukrainian: `docs/content-values.md` (the owner of a value, `entity`, CHECK, functional unique, the rule "a query of all values of a field chooses the owner") and `docs/content-model.md` (the section on cascades). Check the validity of the links in `docs/README.md`

## 2. Registry of system fields and backfill

- [x] 2.1 Create the class of the registry of system fields (next to `FieldTypeRegistry`): key, value type, name, kinds, owners (`node`, `type`), weight, translatability, requiredness for `title` and the seven fields from `specs/content-model`; methods "fields of the kind", "keys of system fields", "whether the field belongs to the owner". PHPDoc in English with `@example`. Check with a unit test of the registry (the list by kind `content`/`page`/`block`, owners, a non-existent key)
- [x] 2.2 `ContentType::booted()` creates the system fields from the registry instead of the hard-coded `title` (the same transaction of `save()`, `title` remains `weight = 0`, required); `ContentField::assertValid()` and `StoreContentFieldRequest` reject a new **non-system** field with the key of a system one, and the creation of a system field bypasses this rule; `RESERVED_KEYS` remains the keys of the service columns. Check with Feature tests: a type `content` has seven fields, `page` — four, `block` — only `title`; the key `meta_title` for a user field is rejected; the existing tests `ContentType*`/`ContentField*` are green
- [x] 2.3 Backfill migration: a snapshot of the list inside the migration; adds the missing fields to the existing types by kind (`weight` after the largest weight of the type), in a transaction; on a conflict with a user field it fails before any changes with the list of types and keys; `down()` deletes the system fields of metadata together with the values. Check with a test on a database with types of three kinds (fields added, existing values and fields unchanged) and a conflict test; manually `migrate:fresh --seed` on MySQL
- [x] 2.4 Update the page of the fields of a type: the system fields of metadata and section are shown as system ones (without deletion, `type`, `is_multiple`, `is_required` are locked) — check whether the existing `is_system` checks already cover this, and fix only the difference. Run `e2e/admin-content-fields.spec.js` and fix the expectations that depend on the number of fields in a type
- [x] 2.5 Update the documentation in Ukrainian: `docs/content-model.md` (the registry of system fields, the matrix of kinds, the owners of values, the reserved keys of system fields, the backfill and conflicts, the field `title`), `docs/admin-content-fields.md` (reserved keys, system fields of metadata in the table of fields). Check `grep -rn "RESERVED_KEYS" docs/` for consistency

## 3. Writing and reading values of a type

- [x] 3.1 Add a value object of the owner (a record or a type) and move `ContentValueWriter::write/validate/replace` to it: suitable fields are derived from the registry, a field that does not belong to the owner is rejected with an error under the key of the field, the rows contain `entity`, the columns of the record or `NULL`. The public signatures for `ContentNode` remain compatible; `ContentNodeCreator` and the controllers do not change. PHPDoc in English with `@example`. Check the existing writing tests (`docker compose exec app php artisan test --filter='ContentValue|ContentNode'`) without regressions
- [x] 3.2 `ContentValueReader`: a method of reading the values of a type by language (missing — `null`, without substitution of the base one, an unknown key or a key foreign to the owner — `ValidationException`) and the unchanged batch reading of records. PHPDoc with `@example`. Check with Feature tests: reading by languages (`default`, `en`), a missing translation, `section_title` not available for a record, `title` not available for a type, the number of requests for reading records has not changed
- [x] 3.3 `ContentFieldController::valuedKeys` selects only `entity = 'node'`, `ContentField::hasStoredValues` remains for both owners. Check with tests: a field with values of the type only is not deleted, but is not considered filled in the records; sorting, filtering and searching of records of a type do not depend on the values of the type (`ContentNodeQuery`)
- [x] 3.4 Update the documentation in Ukrainian: `docs/content-values.md` (writing and reading for two owners, translations, errors), `docs/content-querying.md` (the values of a type do not affect the selection, isolation by the owner). Check the links

